+-----------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running ${PKGSTEM} on OpenBSD
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------

To make groff manual page output as similar as possible to mandoc(1)
output, the following two groff features have been disabled by
default in man(7) and mdoc(7) manual pages: adjustment of text to
the right margin and hyphenation.

The following chamges have been made to fix regressions in the 1.23 release:
 * The base paragraph indentation in manual pages is set to 5n, not to 7n.
 * The title in manual page header lines is set in roman,
   not in italic font.
 * Manual page names marked up with the mdoc(7) .Nm macro are always
   set in bold, not in roman font, including in the NAME section.
 * Manual page cross references are set in roman, not in italic font.
 * Literal text in mdoc(7) is set in constant width roman,
   not in bold font.
 * Set .Sx in italic font, not in roman font with quotes.
 * Do not set the mdoc(7) date to "UNDATED".
 * Omit empty parantheses in the header when no section number is given.
 * All tail arguments of .ME and .UE macros are correctly printed.
 * Vertical spacing before .HP macros is reduced to the correct amount.
 * The .OP macro does not pick a wrong font when called without arguments.

The following change has been made to fix an older groff regression:
 * .Dt puts the architecture name in parentheses after the volume
   title in the header line, not before the volume title.

The following improvements have been made.
It is expected that they will be pushed upstream later:
 * Support .Lb in the synopsis.
 * The .Bx macro now supports arbitrary second arguments.
 * If the first argument of .TH is empty, set the title to "UNTITLED".

Because the OpenBSD manual pages do not yet consistently escape
hyphen-minus and accents characters in a typographically correct
way, unescaped hyphen-minus and accent ASCII input characters are
mapped to ASCII output glyphs in the traditional way.

To suit the taste of OpenBSD developers, one mdoc(7) formatting
detail has been changed with respect to the upstream distribution:
Title lines use an n-dash, not an m-dash between the manual page
name and the manual page description.
